  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of life Saving Gender Based Violence(VBG) and Sexual and Reproductive Health services (SRH) for migrant  women and adolescents in Dari&#xe9;n</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The key objective of this UNFPA project is to the provision of integrated sexual and reproductive health (SRH) and gender-based violence (GBV) services to women in transit or at the temporary Migrant Reception Station (ETRMs) in Darien. CERF allocation will improve access to essential sexual and reproductive health (SRH) services such as emergency obstetric and neonatal care, safe childbirth, family planning, and care for survivors of sexual violence. UNFPA provides GBV prevention and response services. The project targets 46,331 people, including 16,216 women, and 30,115 children. 1,000 persons with disabilities are also supported.</narrative>
  </description>
